  "reply": "I rewrote `parseDuration` in `src/duration.ts`, and `bun test` passes (26 tests, 0 failures). That is the only file I changed.\n\n- **What it accepts:** one or more components of digits followed by `h`, `m`, `s` or `ms`, in strictly descending order, with optional whitespace between components and at both ends. For example, `\"1h 30m\"` and `\"1h30m\"` both parse.\n- **What it rejects:** empty or whitespace-only input, duplicate or out-of-order units, signs, fractions and any other junk all throw `RangeError`. A space between a number and its unit, like `\"1 h\"`, is also rejected, since you only allowed whitespace between components.\n- **Overflow:** the total is summed as a `BigInt`, so any total above `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` throws `RangeError` rather than losing precision.\n- **API:** the `parseDuration` export keeps the same signature, and the library stays dependency-free as `CLAUDE.md` requires.\n\nI didn't add any tests of my own. The existing tests cover the old `ms`-only behavior and the new cases only as far as those 26 go.",
